1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,432
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,433 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,174 --> 00:00:05,234
(Episode 57)

4
00:00:11,864 --> 00:00:13,165
Surprise!

5
00:00:14,718 --> 00:00:16,040
Yeong Ju?

6
00:00:17,482 --> 00:00:19,672
Yeong Ju.

7
00:00:21,831 --> 00:00:23,786
Ji Ni was locked in a storage room?

8
00:00:24,746 --> 00:00:26,773
Her middle school friend Do Hee...

9
00:00:27,011 --> 00:00:29,112
must have been jealous of Ji Ni's talent.

10
00:00:30,015 --> 00:00:32,712
She mocked her as a mistress's daughter
and bullied her at school.

11
00:00:32,832 --> 00:00:36,359
But she's out of the storage room now,
thanks to you.

12
00:00:37,299 --> 00:00:38,773
But she still says she doesn't want love.

13
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:40,999
She's so stubborn.

14
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:44,700
Still, tell her how you feel again.

15
00:00:44,832 --> 00:00:47,733
If you two could run together
with that much energy,

16
00:00:48,056 --> 00:00:50,136
I think she has some feelings for you.

17
00:00:50,304 --> 00:00:53,009
- Really?
- Isn't it worth telling her?

18
00:00:53,472 --> 00:00:55,935
If she says no, accept it,

19
00:00:56,185 --> 00:00:58,740
and if she needs time, wait.

20
00:01:00,037 --> 00:01:03,892
Couples who fall in love at first sight
and confess like Romeo and Juliet...

21
00:01:03,994 --> 00:01:05,786
probably don't exist.

22
00:01:07,544 --> 00:01:09,129
I wish it could be like that.

23
00:01:09,912 --> 00:01:12,915
The thought of us confessing our love
makes me happy.

24
00:01:13,977 --> 00:01:15,211
Should I ask her for you?

25
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:16,618
No, I should do it myself.

26
00:01:17,471 --> 00:01:19,115
I'll do it and face the outcome myself.

27
00:01:21,205 --> 00:01:23,067
Found you!

28
00:01:23,632 --> 00:01:27,135
Yeong Ju, why are you here?
I've been looking all over for you.

29
00:01:28,204 --> 00:01:29,622
That's what love is like.

30
00:01:36,978 --> 00:01:39,647
You asked her for love advice?
Good for you.

31
00:01:40,465 --> 00:01:42,730
Yeong Ju's a good person to talk to.

32
00:02:03,411 --> 00:02:05,935
Even if I don't say it,
you have my support.

33
00:02:06,612 --> 00:02:09,185
I was only thinking
about how Do Hee was making me suffer.

34
00:02:09,210 --> 00:02:11,160
You must be hurting just as much as I am.

35
00:02:16,672 --> 00:02:17,672
Say ah.

36
00:02:20,935 --> 00:02:23,211
Aren't you glad you got married?
You're happy, right?

37
00:02:24,045 --> 00:02:25,722
Yes, I am.

38
00:02:27,265 --> 00:02:30,532
But who does Ji Hu take after?

39
00:02:30,672 --> 00:02:32,882
He doesn't take after his mom or dad.

40
00:02:32,907 --> 00:02:34,770
Not in his tastes or his personality.

41
00:02:35,135 --> 00:02:36,323
He takes after me.

42
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:37,730
Handsome and purehearted.

43
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:40,946
You shouldn't say that about yourself.

44
00:02:40,948 --> 00:02:42,812
Why not? It's just you.

45
00:02:44,004 --> 00:02:47,095
I think they said
he takes after his maternal grandma.

46
00:02:47,674 --> 00:02:51,083
His grandma raised him for a long time.

47
00:02:51,085 --> 00:02:53,050
Sun Kyung had
severe postpartum depression.

48
00:02:54,252 --> 00:02:55,252
Sa Bin.

49
00:02:55,818 --> 00:02:58,187
Maybe I shouldn't have quit singing class.

50
00:02:59,238 --> 00:03:01,302
Should I do some cleaning at the clinic?

51
00:03:01,578 --> 00:03:03,527
Being home all the time drains my energy.

52
00:03:03,552 --> 00:03:06,820
Su Yeon's there too.
Having me there could make things awkward.

53
00:03:06,845 --> 00:03:08,233
True.

54
00:03:08,257 --> 00:03:11,740
Having you and Sun Kyung there
could make things awkward...

55
00:03:11,764 --> 00:03:12,888
for Su Yeon.

56
00:03:12,912 --> 00:03:14,113
I'd love having you there.

57
00:03:14,138 --> 00:03:16,118
Then come to work with me tomorrow.

58
00:03:16,143 --> 00:03:19,125
We should ask Sun Kyung first.

59
00:03:19,149 --> 00:03:21,602
You're right. That would be best.

60
00:03:21,732 --> 00:03:23,703
She's the boss at home.

61
00:03:23,728 --> 00:03:26,012
But I'm the boss at the clinic.

62
00:03:26,412 --> 00:03:28,845
You can just relax there.

63
00:03:34,328 --> 00:03:35,403
Recharging happiness?

64
00:03:36,886 --> 00:03:38,304
Fully recharged.

65
00:03:43,049 --> 00:03:44,589
(O Reum's Banh Xeo)

66
00:03:46,223 --> 00:03:48,229
So this is what a professional can do.

67
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:52,356
I didn't have time to have it
professionally made,

68
00:03:52,358 --> 00:03:54,264
so I painted it on fabric myself.

69
00:03:55,305 --> 00:03:56,570
It's wonderful.

70
00:03:56,999 --> 00:03:58,223
I really appreciate it.

71
00:03:58,698 --> 00:04:00,554
I'm glad you like it.

72
00:04:00,884 --> 00:04:04,248
I got nervous
when it was time to give it to you.

73
00:04:04,692 --> 00:04:07,314
Mai will love it when she sees it too.

74
00:04:11,703 --> 00:04:14,558
How can I thank you for this?

75
00:04:15,389 --> 00:04:16,803
It's your birthday gift.

76
00:04:17,158 --> 00:04:19,109
I heard today's your birthday.

77
00:04:19,466 --> 00:04:20,466
Thank you.

78
00:04:28,005 --> 00:04:29,852
- Didn't you get me anything?
- I did.

79
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,391
But I won't give it to you.

80
00:04:43,938 --> 00:04:45,625
You prepared all this?

81
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:48,004
Come in. I just need to serve the rice.

82
00:04:49,305 --> 00:04:51,436
You made all this, Mom?

83
00:04:51,566 --> 00:04:53,116
Didn't Yeong Ju stop by?

84
00:04:53,734 --> 00:04:55,879
- Did my mom stop by?
- No!

85
00:04:55,904 --> 00:04:58,486
I cooked everything. Why do you doubt me?

86
00:04:59,011 --> 00:05:00,349
I'll cook for your birthday too.

87
00:05:00,574 --> 00:05:02,816
It's in two days.
I'll do even better than today.

88
00:05:03,559 --> 00:05:04,688
Don't.

89
00:05:04,713 --> 00:05:07,310
- We had it today. Why have it again?
- So it's your birthday.

90
00:05:07,798 --> 00:05:10,026
I don't mind having it again. Thank you.

91
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:11,226
What?

92
00:05:11,546 --> 00:05:14,265
That's right. Eat up and be grateful.

93
00:05:15,359 --> 00:05:18,642
I didn't think I'd ever see this happen.

94
00:05:19,098 --> 00:05:20,327
You don't remember, do you?

95
00:05:20,352 --> 00:05:23,914
I made the rice cakes
for your first birthday party too.

96
00:05:25,893 --> 00:05:26,893
Mom!

97
00:05:28,066 --> 00:05:30,052
Sorry.

98
00:05:30,211 --> 00:05:32,480
I just got lost in old memories...

99
00:05:33,011 --> 00:05:37,225
Let's agree not to discuss
anything from more than three months ago.

100
00:05:37,249 --> 00:05:40,026
I promise I won't.

101
00:05:41,170 --> 00:05:42,541
Yes, please don't bring it up.

102
00:05:42,948 --> 00:05:45,033
Nothing from over three months ago.

103
00:05:45,058 --> 00:05:46,604
That's our first house rule.

104
00:05:46,907 --> 00:05:49,439
- Okay.
- Mom, you're unbelievable.

105
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:54,289
Yeong Ju will probably come tonight
and make another birthday meal.

106
00:05:54,314 --> 00:05:55,517
Let's save the candles for then.

107
00:05:55,852 --> 00:05:56,870
Is mom coming?

108
00:05:57,792 --> 00:05:58,792
I haven't heard from her.

109
00:06:02,446 --> 00:06:06,270
Did you meet
the person who contacted you yesterday?

110
00:06:08,248 --> 00:06:10,253
Yes, but it wasn't the right person.

111
00:06:11,369 --> 00:06:12,601
I see.

112
00:06:15,631 --> 00:06:17,444
(O Reum's Banh Xeo)

113
00:06:21,879 --> 00:06:23,341
Do you really like it that much?

114
00:06:26,005 --> 00:06:27,900
Your birthday's made you pretty smug.

115
00:06:27,986 --> 00:06:30,911
You'd practically hang a banner
on your gate for your own birthday.

116
00:06:30,936 --> 00:06:32,442
You make a bigger fuss than anyone.

117
00:06:33,745 --> 00:06:36,198
You love basketball,
but you can't play because of me.

118
00:06:36,534 --> 00:06:39,471
Until Mai comes back,
be single again for a while.

119
00:06:39,629 --> 00:06:42,183
Work out and work hard at the shop,

120
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,530
and get back in shape. Like me.

121
00:06:44,693 --> 00:06:46,560
Thank you.

122
00:06:46,874 --> 00:06:47,874
I'll put them to good use.

123
00:06:48,695 --> 00:06:51,205
I booked a table
at your father-in-law's restaurant.

124
00:06:51,318 --> 00:06:52,767
- Don't be late.
- Only us?

125
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:54,553
Why? Should I invite mom too?

126
00:06:54,857 --> 00:06:55,857
No.

127
00:06:55,951 --> 00:06:57,819
We have no idea how things are for her.

128
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,122
She'll come when she's ready.

129
00:07:00,392 --> 00:07:02,621
Still, I thought she'd call this morning.

130
00:07:02,646 --> 00:07:04,015
You sure expect a lot.

131
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:06,299
By the way,

132
00:07:06,954 --> 00:07:08,737
shouldn't you and Ji Ni be more at ease?

133
00:07:08,755 --> 00:07:09,755
I'm fine.

134
00:07:10,032 --> 00:07:11,303
It's not on my mind.

135
00:07:11,805 --> 00:07:14,025
Ji Ni still seems upset with me,

136
00:07:14,052 --> 00:07:17,691
but honestly, we're doing fine.
What more could you want?

137
00:07:30,758 --> 00:07:32,128
What are you doing here?

138
00:07:34,325 --> 00:07:36,367
I said we should stop this.

139
00:07:36,891 --> 00:07:39,593
Just because we're not fake dating,
we can't go to work together?

140
00:07:39,718 --> 00:07:41,454
Is that all our relationship means?

141
00:07:41,996 --> 00:07:42,996
I'm sorry.

142
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:44,716
I only want to see you at work.

143
00:07:45,151 --> 00:07:46,151
Could it be...

144
00:07:46,764 --> 00:07:48,112
you want to stop pretending...

145
00:07:48,458 --> 00:07:51,118
because of me, not Do Hee?

146
00:07:52,026 --> 00:07:53,026
Do you dislike me?

147
00:07:53,112 --> 00:07:55,142
What are you saying?

148
00:07:55,646 --> 00:07:57,948
You know I have feelings for you.

149
00:07:58,571 --> 00:07:59,571
Are you uncomfortable?

150
00:08:00,195 --> 00:08:01,640
I'm not exactly comfortable.

151
00:08:02,605 --> 00:08:05,634
I don't know why you're doing this
when you know I'll say no.

152
00:08:06,431 --> 00:08:08,511
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

153
00:08:08,608 --> 00:08:10,408
- See you at work.
- Ji Ni.

154
00:08:11,285 --> 00:08:12,919
Please don't start this so early.

155
00:08:13,152 --> 00:08:14,947
The thought of love makes my skin crawl.

156
00:08:14,972 --> 00:08:16,190
How many times must I say it?

157
00:08:16,215 --> 00:08:17,889
Why do you keep pushing me to this point?

158
00:08:36,061 --> 00:08:38,862
You've all seen the sample
of the easy-read book I mentioned, right?

159
00:08:38,864 --> 00:08:40,805
Yes, the paper is thin and lightweight,

160
00:08:40,829 --> 00:08:43,847
so people could enjoy a casual read
if we put them at highway rest stops.

161
00:08:43,872 --> 00:08:45,239
Since our CEO has plenty of money,

162
00:08:45,263 --> 00:08:48,393
it's great that we can try new things
without worrying about sales.

163
00:08:48,792 --> 00:08:51,276
I suppose publishing takes
someone with those resources.

164
00:08:51,432 --> 00:08:53,199
No one really reads books these days.

165
00:08:53,223 --> 00:08:54,299
Instead of this project,

166
00:08:54,336 --> 00:08:57,333
why not target
people who are already into books?

167
00:08:58,145 --> 00:08:59,421
Why not do both?

168
00:09:00,151 --> 00:09:02,371
We're a new publishing company,
so we should take more risks...

169
00:09:02,396 --> 00:09:04,092
We're not exactly a startup.

170
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:06,139
What kind of risks can we take
in such a conservative market?

171
00:09:07,378 --> 00:09:09,829
It seems a bit reckless.

172
00:09:13,018 --> 00:09:17,313
Then let's move forward with both.

173
00:09:19,111 --> 00:09:22,305
Ji Sung and I can work
on the easy-read book,

174
00:09:22,443 --> 00:09:24,709
while Tae O and Mi Joo
prepare for the book fair.

175
00:09:25,381 --> 00:09:26,381
And you?

176
00:09:26,701 --> 00:09:29,916
I'll work on some designs
for the book fair merchandise.

177
00:09:30,339 --> 00:09:31,339
Sounds good.

178
00:09:39,507 --> 00:09:40,951
Birthday lunch?

179
00:09:41,896 --> 00:09:43,581
You two go ahead. I'll...

180
00:09:45,830 --> 00:09:47,247
Okay, I understand. I'll be there.

181
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Okay.

182
00:09:51,032 --> 00:09:52,107
Whose birthday is it?

183
00:09:52,622 --> 00:09:54,862
I heard you. I wasn't eavesdropping.

184
00:09:56,255 --> 00:09:58,673
Your auntie's oldest son.

185
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:01,829
You must be getting closer.
You even got invited to his birthday.

186
00:10:02,676 --> 00:10:04,926
- It's a little awkward.
- He's O Reum's dad, after all.

187
00:10:05,050 --> 00:10:06,050
Just relax and go.

188
00:10:06,543 --> 00:10:07,660
O Reum?

189
00:10:09,256 --> 00:10:10,256
Okay.

190
00:10:10,952 --> 00:10:13,124
By the way, did something happen
between you and Tae O?

191
00:10:13,752 --> 00:10:15,132
You two haven't even been coming
to work together.

192
00:10:15,832 --> 00:10:18,109
We decided
to stop pretending we were dating.

193
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:20,741
Why?

194
00:10:21,758 --> 00:10:23,311
You don't have to tell me
if you don't want to.

195
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:28,832
I didn't want to put myself through
something uncomfortable...

196
00:10:29,063 --> 00:10:31,947
just to prove myself to other people.

197
00:10:32,756 --> 00:10:33,756
I agree.

198
00:10:34,282 --> 00:10:35,364
You've gotten stronger.

199
00:10:37,091 --> 00:10:40,105
Ji Hu, stop going on matchmaking dates.
You're already busy with work.

200
00:10:40,639 --> 00:10:43,242
Let them talk. So what if it's unfair?

201
00:10:50,911 --> 00:10:51,919
Tae O.

202
00:11:04,965 --> 00:11:08,863
Just sign here.

203
00:11:22,371 --> 00:11:24,942
- Now...
- Cha Song Studio?

204
00:11:25,675 --> 00:11:26,675
Exactly!

205
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:30,657
Good to see you, Seung Woo.
So we're partners now?

206
00:11:32,244 --> 00:11:34,809
I'll go file the registration now.

207
00:11:37,108 --> 00:11:38,819
- I'm counting on you.
- Sure.

208
00:11:40,207 --> 00:11:43,544
What a relief!

209
00:11:43,546 --> 00:11:45,748
I told you to do it sooner.
So you two ended up as partners?

210
00:11:46,135 --> 00:11:47,409
You can do it yourself later.

211
00:11:47,434 --> 00:11:50,320
I'll take care of things myself,
so stop dropping by.

212
00:11:50,821 --> 00:11:51,960
It's my company.

213
00:11:52,719 --> 00:11:54,534
Hey, I...

214
00:11:54,558 --> 00:11:58,108
I've got trauma from signing papers
and then being treated like a stranger.

215
00:11:58,133 --> 00:12:01,383
That Attorney Byeon?

216
00:12:02,225 --> 00:12:03,647
Are you still looking for him?

217
00:12:03,685 --> 00:12:06,470
How could I not?
He ran off with all my money.

218
00:12:08,231 --> 00:12:11,533
I'm not really interested
in digging up the past anymore.

219
00:12:12,072 --> 00:12:14,831
Seung Hyun and mom are looking into it,

220
00:12:14,855 --> 00:12:16,430
so I'm just staying out of it.

221
00:12:17,378 --> 00:12:19,789
Even if I find him,
it won't undo what happened to me.

222
00:12:26,425 --> 00:12:27,520
Welcome.

223
00:12:35,044 --> 00:12:36,791
I only had seaweed soup this morning.

224
00:12:37,284 --> 00:12:39,703
It's my birthday.
I should eat a proper meal.

225
00:12:40,441 --> 00:12:41,441
Sit down.

226
00:12:46,158 --> 00:12:47,525
Here's your order.

227
00:12:48,157 --> 00:12:49,527
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

228
00:12:51,971 --> 00:12:54,683
If you don't even like him,
why pretend you're dating?

229
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:56,633
Pretend you're dating?

230
00:12:57,556 --> 00:12:58,877
How did you know?

231
00:12:59,399 --> 00:13:00,704
I happened to hear about it.

232
00:13:03,265 --> 00:13:05,112
The woman Ji Hu was dating...

233
00:13:05,686 --> 00:13:09,112
posted online
accusing me of stealing him from her.

234
00:13:10,431 --> 00:13:14,096
To avoid any misunderstandings,
Tae O stepped in to protect me.

235
00:13:14,121 --> 00:13:16,207
He'd protect you
even if he didn't like you?

236
00:13:16,338 --> 00:13:17,614
He likes you.

237
00:13:18,418 --> 00:13:19,925
That doesn't change anything.

238
00:13:20,292 --> 00:13:22,215
Why are you so determined
not to fall in love?

239
00:13:23,778 --> 00:13:25,518
If you were me, would you?

240
00:13:26,169 --> 00:13:27,169
What's wrong with being you?

241
00:13:32,592 --> 00:13:35,502
If I speak up, people point fingers
and say I'm just like my mom.

242
00:13:36,938 --> 00:13:39,490
If I keep quiet,
they call me well-behaved.

243
00:13:40,769 --> 00:13:42,457
But if I hold my head up,
they call me shameless.

244
00:13:44,858 --> 00:13:46,882
So it's just easier that way.

245
00:13:48,312 --> 00:13:50,464
It's your life, no matter what
other people say.

246
00:13:51,041 --> 00:13:54,165
Just because dad was that way
doesn't mean you have to be.

247
00:13:55,165 --> 00:13:57,354
That's easy for you two to say.

248
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:58,655
How are you any different?

249
00:13:59,389 --> 00:14:01,028
We grew up without a dad.

250
00:14:01,605 --> 00:14:03,945
And you had dad all to yourself.

251
00:14:03,972 --> 00:14:05,429
What do you have to complain about?

252
00:14:06,532 --> 00:14:07,532
Seung Hyun...

253
00:14:07,597 --> 00:14:10,323
Why dwell on what you're missing
instead of what you have?

254
00:14:10,992 --> 00:14:13,535
Honestly, you sound pretty ungrateful.

255
00:14:15,631 --> 00:14:17,700
You two were proud
even when you were lonely.

256
00:14:18,383 --> 00:14:19,567
I'm not.

257
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:25,053
You said we'd have a birthday meal.
Why are we talking about this?

258
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:28,315
Ji Ni!

259
00:14:33,778 --> 00:14:34,898
What's wrong with you?

260
00:14:35,112 --> 00:14:36,399
Did you have to go that far?

261
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,080
I don't know.

262
00:14:39,732 --> 00:14:41,266
I've just been angry at everything lately.

263
00:14:41,805 --> 00:14:44,798
I used to be able to hold it in,
but I don't want to anymore.

264
00:14:47,472 --> 00:14:49,997
Seung Hyun, let's try counseling.

265
00:14:50,305 --> 00:14:53,445
You've been through too much
to keep handling it on your own.

266
00:14:58,145 --> 00:14:59,302
I've been thinking about it too.

267
00:15:12,219 --> 00:15:17,046
(O Reum's Banh Xeo)

268
00:15:26,478 --> 00:15:28,749
Hello. Are you open?

269
00:15:29,110 --> 00:15:30,838
No. I just parked here for a minute.

270
00:15:31,365 --> 00:15:34,609
I came looking for a Vietnamese drink,

271
00:15:34,703 --> 00:15:36,212
so could I just buy one?

272
00:15:38,346 --> 00:15:40,998
- Sure. Just a moment.
- Thank you.

273
00:15:45,138 --> 00:15:46,138
Here you go.

274
00:15:46,291 --> 00:15:47,798
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

275
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:49,198
I knew this would happen.

276
00:15:49,332 --> 00:15:50,563
You said you weren't selling.

277
00:15:50,938 --> 00:15:51,938
Then why did you sell it?

278
00:15:52,112 --> 00:15:53,557
I'll move the car soon. Don't worry.

279
00:15:53,558 --> 00:15:55,023
But you just made a sale.

280
00:15:55,025 --> 00:15:56,125
I saw the whole thing.

281
00:15:56,218 --> 00:15:58,293
You'll say you're not selling,

282
00:15:58,467 --> 00:15:59,891
then start again once I go inside.

283
00:16:00,278 --> 00:16:01,278
Move it, now!

284
00:16:02,305 --> 00:16:03,878
What's this? Move!

285
00:16:04,678 --> 00:16:05,700
What are you doing?

286
00:16:07,208 --> 00:16:09,011
What on earth is this? What a pain.

287
00:16:13,411 --> 00:16:14,637
I said, stop it!

288
00:16:17,752 --> 00:16:18,945
You little punk!

289
00:16:19,185 --> 00:16:21,735
They weren't selling anything.
We were just eating here.

290
00:16:22,162 --> 00:16:23,535
Call it in! What are you waiting for?

291
00:16:24,642 --> 00:16:26,090
I already did. Get to the station!

292
00:16:26,497 --> 00:16:27,497
Go!

293
00:16:28,085 --> 00:16:29,465
What did I do wrong?

294
00:16:38,992 --> 00:16:41,366
I need to talk to you for a minute.

295
00:16:45,532 --> 00:16:48,214
I don't think
all three of us need to stay here,

296
00:16:48,535 --> 00:16:51,947
so I was thinking
of going to the clinic to help Sa Bin.

297
00:16:51,948 --> 00:16:53,042
What are you talking about?

298
00:16:53,878 --> 00:16:56,251
There are more of us now,
and you want the two of us to do it all?

299
00:16:59,078 --> 00:17:01,692
There's more outside.
Please bring in some more.

300
00:17:10,171 --> 00:17:12,458
We're running low on kimchi
before we make the next batch.

301
00:17:13,825 --> 00:17:15,291
Su Yeon, hand me that knife.

302
00:17:17,238 --> 00:17:19,914
Su Yeon, Yeong Ju wants that knife
over there.

303
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,469
Sure.

304
00:17:23,851 --> 00:17:25,227
What are you doing?

305
00:17:25,908 --> 00:17:26,908
What?

306
00:17:27,937 --> 00:17:30,504
Su Yeon, you picked good cabbages.

307
00:17:30,692 --> 00:17:31,692
Right?

308
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,573
Call me when you season them.

309
00:17:33,672 --> 00:17:35,658
- I'll taste the seasoning.
- Okay.

310
00:17:39,192 --> 00:17:40,292
What's gotten into you?

311
00:17:40,838 --> 00:17:42,838
Please stop picking on me.

312
00:17:51,345 --> 00:17:52,345
Yeah, what is it?

313
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:54,572
The police station?

314
00:17:55,717 --> 00:17:56,817
Why is Seung Hyun there?

315
00:17:58,178 --> 00:18:00,605
Goodness. Okay. I'll be there soon.

316
00:18:01,726 --> 00:18:04,351
- I'm going to step out for a bit.
- Okay.

317
00:18:05,038 --> 00:18:06,311
Yeong Ju, why are you leaving?

318
00:18:07,092 --> 00:18:08,092
Why is she leaving?

319
00:18:08,325 --> 00:18:09,325
She isn't making kimchi?

320
00:18:09,425 --> 00:18:13,016
No, Seung Hyun's at the police station.
Her oldest son.

321
00:18:13,351 --> 00:18:15,025
The police station?
Did he get into a fight?

322
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:16,725
Of course not.

323
00:18:16,726 --> 00:18:19,210
He's so mild-mannered.
He'd never get into a fight.

324
00:18:19,212 --> 00:18:21,468
Then why would
a civil servant be at the police station?

325
00:18:21,616 --> 00:18:23,205
He quit his government job.

326
00:18:23,511 --> 00:18:26,350
Now he drives a food truck
and sells Vietnamese food.

327
00:18:26,352 --> 00:18:27,879
Really?

328
00:18:29,427 --> 00:18:31,583
My goodness, No Yeong Ju.

329
00:18:31,811 --> 00:18:33,051
What are we going to do?

330
00:18:34,798 --> 00:18:36,985
Come over here and tell me what happened.

331
00:18:41,292 --> 00:18:44,438
The name is Cha Seung Hyun.

332
00:18:49,185 --> 00:18:50,185
Seung Hyun.

333
00:18:53,651 --> 00:18:54,698
You didn't have to come.

334
00:18:55,378 --> 00:18:56,378
What's the matter with you?

335
00:18:56,515 --> 00:18:58,810
I'm not a kid who needs a guardian.
Why'd you call her?

336
00:18:58,812 --> 00:19:00,792
They don't respect me
because I'm the younger brother.

337
00:19:03,252 --> 00:19:05,031
They asked if anyone else was home.

338
00:19:05,298 --> 00:19:07,211
- You're his mother?
- Yes.

339
00:19:07,498 --> 00:19:08,691
What happened?

340
00:19:08,952 --> 00:19:10,571
They said he got into a fight.

341
00:19:10,573 --> 00:19:12,780
He's never done anything like this.

342
00:19:12,782 --> 00:19:13,944
It's a pretty simple situation.

343
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:16,103
The truck is properly licensed,

344
00:19:16,156 --> 00:19:18,250
but he was selling in an area
where food trucks aren't allowed.

345
00:19:18,252 --> 00:19:21,111
And he pushed someone in the process.

346
00:19:21,198 --> 00:19:22,911
I only sold one drink.

347
00:19:22,912 --> 00:19:25,019
Whether it was one or two,
you shouldn't have sold any.

348
00:19:25,558 --> 00:19:27,571
And why did you push someone?

349
00:19:27,818 --> 00:19:29,965
What's gotten into you?
That's not like you.

350
00:19:30,132 --> 00:19:32,827
The victim wasn't seriously injured,
and he's willing to settle,

351
00:19:32,874 --> 00:19:34,037
so let's resolve this peacefully.

352
00:19:34,785 --> 00:19:36,591
We're sorry. Thank you.

353
00:19:37,752 --> 00:19:39,751
Don't let your temper control you.

354
00:19:40,032 --> 00:19:41,298
Try to keep your cool.

355
00:19:48,071 --> 00:19:49,878
Thank you. Take care.

356
00:19:52,792 --> 00:19:55,138
If you're going to sell food,
do it in the designated area.

357
00:19:55,305 --> 00:19:57,398
Why did the three of you even go there?

358
00:19:57,532 --> 00:19:59,129
It was Seung Hyun's birthday,
so we went there to eat.

359
00:20:00,077 --> 00:20:01,077
Birthday?

360
00:20:02,483 --> 00:20:04,883
- That's fine.
- Are you really okay?

361
00:20:05,752 --> 00:20:07,705
You always say you're fine,
and look what happened.

362
00:20:09,098 --> 00:20:10,318
Should I say I'm not okay?

363
00:20:11,052 --> 00:20:13,460
Ji Ni's mom made me seaweed soup
for breakfast, and I ate it.

364
00:20:13,635 --> 00:20:15,518
Then we went out for lunch together,
and this happened.

365
00:20:15,612 --> 00:20:17,012
Why wouldn't I be okay?

366
00:20:17,225 --> 00:20:18,505
I'm completely fine!

367
00:20:21,125 --> 00:20:22,613
Look who's getting angry now.

368
00:20:22,841 --> 00:20:24,193
- Seung Hyun!
- Mom.

369
00:20:25,197 --> 00:20:26,197
Don't.

370
00:20:27,612 --> 00:20:29,198
Did I tell him to start a business?

371
00:20:29,378 --> 00:20:31,698
He quit his job at the post office
and started this himself.

372
00:20:32,885 --> 00:20:34,820
Why is he acting like this?

373
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:38,727
It's okay. Let's go.

374
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,196
Let's go.

375
00:20:52,252 --> 00:20:53,885
- Who is it?
- What?

376
00:20:55,572 --> 00:20:58,342
Is this Cha Seung Hyun's house?

377
00:20:58,462 --> 00:21:00,612
Yes. Who are you?

378
00:21:00,692 --> 00:21:03,213
Are you the baby's mom
from the motorcycle accident?

379
00:21:03,682 --> 00:21:05,518
I hear you're looking for a witness.

380
00:21:07,771 --> 00:21:10,022
I was wondering
if it was Pumseongak's motorcycle.

381
00:21:10,163 --> 00:21:11,738
- Pumseongak?
- Yeah.

382
00:21:11,819 --> 00:21:14,278
- Back then...
- Hold on.

383
00:21:16,945 --> 00:21:18,771
Let's talk somewhere else.

384
00:21:19,664 --> 00:21:21,970
I was looking for Cha Seung Hyun.

385
00:21:22,838 --> 00:21:23,896
He's my son.

386
00:21:23,965 --> 00:21:25,425
You can talk to me.

387
00:21:25,750 --> 00:21:27,491
- This way.
- Okay.

388
00:21:36,925 --> 00:21:38,778
Where are we...

389
00:21:39,191 --> 00:21:41,978
This is my office.

390
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:44,018
I figured we'd have a lot to talk about.

391
00:21:45,398 --> 00:21:47,705
What do you know about Pumseongak?

392
00:21:47,912 --> 00:21:49,926
After the accident,

393
00:21:49,928 --> 00:21:53,417
I heard
that Pumseongak suddenly moved away.

394
00:21:53,585 --> 00:21:56,765
I wondered if they moved
because of their son's accident.

395
00:21:56,992 --> 00:21:58,371
It was Pumseongak's son, right?

396
00:21:58,636 --> 00:22:00,331
No.

397
00:22:00,642 --> 00:22:03,194
They caught the culprit.
It was someone else.

398
00:22:03,242 --> 00:22:04,697
- What?
- But...

399
00:22:04,997 --> 00:22:07,825
do you know where Pumseongak moved to?

400
00:22:08,965 --> 00:22:10,711
I heard it was Inju.

401
00:22:11,364 --> 00:22:14,090
I came by
to see if you still hadn't found them.

402
00:22:14,185 --> 00:22:16,106
It's been a long time
since I've been here too.

403
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:18,833
Inju.

404
00:22:20,271 --> 00:22:22,298
I remember when the lady's son got hurt,

405
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,671
and she made quite a scene.

406
00:22:26,658 --> 00:22:30,885
But you're not the woman I remember.

407
00:22:31,231 --> 00:22:33,371
She's my sister.

408
00:22:40,305 --> 00:22:42,701
Anyway, I'm glad it got resolved.

409
00:22:42,865 --> 00:22:45,525
Yes. Thank you.

410
00:22:45,785 --> 00:22:48,499
Thank you for coming
all the way here to tell me.

411
00:22:56,878 --> 00:22:59,919
Mom, I think I need to step out for a bit.

412
00:23:00,387 --> 00:23:01,691
Where are you going this late?

413
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:04,165
I can't believe
I forgot Seung Hyun's birthday.

414
00:23:04,398 --> 00:23:06,005
I feel terrible.

415
00:23:06,091 --> 00:23:07,371
You stay here with him.

416
00:23:09,412 --> 00:23:11,701
How old is he? Why would he get upset
over something like that?

417
00:23:12,102 --> 00:23:13,102
Don't worry.

418
00:23:13,858 --> 00:23:16,051
But he's not the same as he used to be.

419
00:23:16,052 --> 00:23:18,698
Yeah. He's been acting kind of strange.

420
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:20,007
Right? That's what I've been feeling too.

421
00:23:20,008 --> 00:23:22,638
You told him to say everything
instead of holding back.

422
00:23:22,639 --> 00:23:24,250
I told him to talk, not hit someone!

423
00:23:24,252 --> 00:23:26,364
He didn't hit anyone.
We were all together.

424
00:23:27,111 --> 00:23:29,691
Anyway, he just needs a little more time.

425
00:23:29,772 --> 00:23:32,151
Mom, don't say anything else. Okay?

426
00:23:34,938 --> 00:23:36,278
I'll be right back, Yeong Ju.

427
00:23:52,412 --> 00:23:54,598
You're here, Yeong Ju? I knew you'd come.

428
00:23:55,078 --> 00:23:57,618
I didn't come because I knew
it was his birthday. I forgot.

429
00:23:59,358 --> 00:24:03,061
I heard you brought him seaweed soup
and a cake. Thank you.

430
00:24:03,562 --> 00:24:05,071
It was nothing.

431
00:24:28,545 --> 00:24:30,371
I had to sneak it past Ji Ni.

432
00:24:31,218 --> 00:24:34,021
What's so great about drinking?
Listen to Ji Ni.

433
00:24:34,942 --> 00:24:36,105
I know.

434
00:24:42,412 --> 00:24:45,008
Yeong Ju, I'll go change my clothes.

435
00:24:45,009 --> 00:24:46,009
Okay.

436
00:25:17,098 --> 00:25:19,571
Why dwell on what you're missing
instead of what you have?

437
00:25:19,772 --> 00:25:21,790
Honestly, you sound pretty ungrateful.

438
00:25:29,805 --> 00:25:31,498
This has completely backfired.

439
00:25:31,978 --> 00:25:36,141
Ji Hu went on matchmaking dates,
and Ji Ni went on a date with a guy.

440
00:25:37,152 --> 00:25:38,826
People are unbelievable.

441
00:25:38,914 --> 00:25:40,656
How did they dig all this up?

442
00:25:40,704 --> 00:25:42,991
- What about Do Hee?
- Her phone's off.

443
00:25:43,292 --> 00:25:46,344
She's already emotionally fragile.
I'm worried about her.

444
00:25:46,345 --> 00:25:49,094
If she's so fragile,
why does she keep lying?

445
00:25:50,227 --> 00:25:51,227
This is driving me crazy.

446
00:25:51,358 --> 00:25:55,045
They're saying they can't believe
what Do Hee showed on the show.

447
00:25:55,171 --> 00:25:56,845
They're saying, "Wasn't it all staged?"

448
00:25:56,971 --> 00:25:59,998
They're making a huge fuss, saying,
"Didn't you deliberately cast her?"

449
00:26:03,412 --> 00:26:04,812
You know where she lives, right?

450
00:26:05,052 --> 00:26:06,172
Go check on her.

451
00:26:07,398 --> 00:26:08,931
I thought about that too.

452
00:26:12,383 --> 00:26:14,718
What's the point of
barging in there right now?

453
00:26:15,258 --> 00:26:16,841
She'll just lie again,

454
00:26:17,049 --> 00:26:18,285
or come up with excuses.

455
00:26:19,205 --> 00:26:21,368
We'll scold her and blame her,

456
00:26:21,815 --> 00:26:23,238
but it'll accomplish nothing.

457
00:26:23,965 --> 00:26:25,218
We need to give her some time,

458
00:26:25,452 --> 00:26:27,618
and let her
figure out how to fix this herself.

459
00:26:28,152 --> 00:26:29,152
How?

460
00:26:29,424 --> 00:26:30,795
As for the claim he left her
for someone else,

461
00:26:31,065 --> 00:26:34,208
we could say it was a side effect
of being devastated when they broke up...

462
00:26:35,102 --> 00:26:36,102
I don't know.

463
00:26:36,625 --> 00:26:37,871
Let's talk about that later.

464
00:26:38,478 --> 00:26:40,922
For now, let's just
let her be alone tonight.

465
00:26:42,163 --> 00:26:43,685
Yeah. Okay.

466
00:26:44,789 --> 00:26:45,789
Seriously...

467
00:26:47,044 --> 00:26:48,644
Get some rest.

468
00:26:48,972 --> 00:26:49,972
We'll talk tomorrow.

469
00:26:51,509 --> 00:26:53,151
Okay. Take care.

470
00:27:08,265 --> 00:27:09,458
I can breathe again.

471
00:27:13,090 --> 00:27:16,970
Let's go!

472
00:27:23,557 --> 00:27:25,744
Make some noise!

473
00:27:35,011 --> 00:27:36,011
I'm hungry!

474
00:27:36,332 --> 00:27:38,238
I'm hungry.
Why do I keep getting so hungry?

475
00:28:30,328 --> 00:28:33,748
(Family Register)

476
00:28:33,749 --> 00:28:34,825
You should've told me.

477
00:28:34,827 --> 00:28:36,142
I'd have lent you the money, at least.

478
00:28:36,143 --> 00:28:38,023
Don't say things like that.
We're perfectly fine.

479
00:28:38,025 --> 00:28:40,005
- Do you have an inferiority complex?
- Honestly...

480
00:28:40,006 --> 00:28:41,883
Why aren't you taking my side these days?

481
00:28:41,885 --> 00:28:42,976
Looks like there's another woman.

482
00:28:42,978 --> 00:28:44,691
They asked if your husband is cheating.

483
00:28:44,692 --> 00:28:47,391
What kind of nonsense is that?
Do you really think that little of me?

484
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,765
After putting me through all this,
they're out going to exhibitions?

485
00:28:49,767 --> 00:28:51,050
She's really getting on my nerves.

486
00:28:51,052 --> 00:28:52,238
What's your relationship with Na Ji Ni?

487
00:28:52,239 --> 00:28:54,959
Director, you're on my side, right?
Stay with me until I fall asleep.

488
00:28:54,961 --> 00:28:55,961
I'm lonely.

489
00:28:56,073 --> 00:28:58,073
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
